1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,480
You don't need 48 button variants.

2
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:05,440
Here's why most component sets get out of control.

3
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:07,760
Variants are for things that change the look.

4
00:00:07,760 --> 00:00:09,520
Type, state, and size.

5
00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:11,680
Primary, hover, disabled.

6
00:00:11,680 --> 00:00:14,400
Properties are for things that change the content.

7
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:18,240
The text, a hidden icon, or which icon is shown.

8
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:20,480
Three types, four states, two sizes,

9
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:22,080
with and without an icon.

10
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:23,840
That's 48 variants.

11
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:26,000
Turn the icon into a Boolean property,

12
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:27,840
and it drops to 24.

13
00:00:27,840 --> 00:00:30,160
Same button, half the variants.

14
00:00:30,160 --> 00:00:32,880
Pro tip, use a text property for the label,

15
00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:36,880
and instance swap for the icon so nobody has to detach.

16
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:37,760
Save this?

17
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:39,360
Variants change the look.

18
00:00:39,360 --> 00:00:41,280
Properties change the content.

19
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:45,920
Learn UX and UI Design Live at Agile Design School.

